  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAUTI ZETU</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAUTI ZETU which means OUR VOICES is a project which aim to amplify the voices of youths/young people with disability to be given achance to participate in decision making processes and influence changes and achieve sustainable development in Singida Municipal and in Tanzania at large. The project also creates a platform to bring together youths with disability twice a year to share experience, learn and raise their voices through interviews and interact with government officials and other stakeholders.The project will also raise concerns on accountability, transparency, participation to development planning and create awareness to the general communities on the position of youths with disabilities to bring and contribute to the country&apos;s development.

SAUTI ZETU project is a creative initiative aimed bring together youth/young people with disability and amplify their voices on how to be engaged and meaningful participate in decision making processes in all levels of development. The project will useacreated platform of youths to exchangeknowledge, skills, share challenges and learn while voicing their views through MPs, social media. Objectives include the ability generate and use data, capacity to mobilize and hold their representatives and decision-makers accountable and sharing of knowledge. Outcome are increase awareness, youths with disability engage on decision making process, access opportunities and influence change</narrative>
  </description>
